rota lap 4164, row 4 -- Earth, the row that breathes in; read through the threshold page and the clock-and-mark foundation, and its sentence carried the lap: the concrete fact outranks the plausible story. The lap that followed was exactly that -- four desks each claiming a number, and the number read off the module rather than off the claim.
think Opened with the round open (already on the anointed order, two logs and nineteen files standing in the dead-letter box and nowhere else) and read the card whole. The lane's own named next work is the several-line interleave in mantra/src/weave.rye, which two prior laps recommended and neither took, because it widens Diff and both read that as a seam wanting a word.
think Before taking a seam I measured the claim the seam rests on: mantra/src/diff.rye's head says the widening "widens a structure Glow's shape is pinned against". That pin is real -- src/shape/shape-mantra-diff-field-count.glow -- so the seam stands. What the measurement turned up beside it is the lap: src/gate/gate-mantra-diff-fields-eq-u32.glow, one directory over, still reads "a Diff's two fields (inserts - deletes)" while the shape beside it moved two to three on 20260906.212206.
think Read the actual counts with tools/fixtures/r/rye_struct_fields_scan.sh --count: Line 4, Weave 2, Diff 3. Read the four gates: line decides 3, weave 2, diff 2, store 3. Two of four decide the opposite of the truth -- they answer 0 for the count their own struct carries and 1 for a count nothing carries.
think Asked what should have caught it and found the shape of the fault. tools/m/mantra_a1_equality_witness.rish asserts "line fields=3 decide exactly"; tools/rye/mantra_a1_line_fields_eq_witness.rye passes "3" to the desk; the desk decides 3; tools/fixtures/m/mantra_a1_equality_control.sh proves the family reds when that number is MOVED. Three copies of one number, agreeing with each other. The sur limbs one directory over had learned this on 20260906 under %500 and the comment saying so is in limb1 and limb3 -- and it stopped at src/shape/.
think Repaired both desks and both Rye witnesses, then closed the class rather than the instance: the number is now read from both sides by one file, tools/fixtures/m/mantra_gate_constant_scan.sh, which the guard calls and the control plants against, so the comparison is written once and neither copy can drift from the other.
obs The number moved and the stamp held. The row booked at %555 off a fetch at 09:47; the rebase forty-five minutes later brought five upstream rows home, so it published at %560 -- the derived spine working exactly as written, and the living card cites the stamp `20260907.094747` rather than either number.
obs The store desk is bound by the same reader on purpose and the comment says why: Store's three fields are all Dir handles, so a struct count answers a directory question exactly. A non-directory field added later reds that leg, which is the honest outcome -- the desk would then want its own reader rather than this one.
obs The scan reports and never gates: it answers ok, constant_disagrees, desk_absent, desk_decides_nothing or struct_unreadable, in words rather than numbers, so no reading of its output can be mistaken for an exit code. Gating stays the witness's job.
obs Not taken, and named rather than swept: the Aurora three and the Caravan one that src/gate/README.md lists beside these four are unrostered AND unbound alike, each pinning a number in another lane's room.
loom roster=hot guards=168 guards_seconds=1199 green=164 red=1 gated=3
obs The one red in the hot pass was standing_equipment on its live_group_plant leg, GREEN alone on the same tree a minute later -- the sixth firing of the concurrency flake the card names across three guards, each of which forks a real service on eight cores.
